# Muta — optional deployment configuration. Copy to `.env` and edit; never commit `.env`.
# Everything here has a safe default, so an empty/absent .env is a valid local dev setup.
# The full variable reference is docs/configuration.md.

# --- Security -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HMAC secret for /v1 bearer tokens. UNSET (default) = dev mode: the token is the student's
# per-device id (an attacker must know a victim's random UUID to act as them). SET = tokens
# are signed and unforgeable — recommended for any shared/LAN deployment. Use a long random
# value, e.g.  openssl rand -hex 32
# MUTA_AUTH_SECRET=

# Postgres password. Default "muta" is fine for a single local box; change it for anything
# reachable by others. The backend DSN tracks this automatically (docker-compose.yml).
# MUTA_DB_PASSWORD=

# --- Logging --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DEBUG | INFO | WARNING | ERROR. Default INFO. Turn on DEBUG without editing code.
# MUTA_LOG_LEVEL=INFO

# --- Cloud boost (OFF unless all three are set) ---------------------------------------
# When online, route chat to a stronger cloud model, falling back to the local engine
# silently. NOTE: this sends student chat history off-device — see docs/privacy-and-data-flows.md
# and get explicit consent before enabling in a school. Keep the API key out of git.
# MUTA_CLOUD_URL=
# MUTA_CLOUD_MODEL=
# MUTA_CLOUD_API_KEY=

# --- Web grounding (OFF unless set) ---------------------------------------------------
# A SearXNG-shaped search endpoint. When set + online + the student opts in, answers are
# grounded with fresh snippets. Sends the student's message text off-device.
# MUTA_SEARCH_URL=

# --- Engine threads (normally leave UNSET) --------------------------------------------
# Empty = llama.cpp picks physical cores (correct on a real x86 target). run.sh sets the
# Apple-VM pins automatically under emulation; only set these to override on a specific box.
# MUTA_RT_N_THREADS=
# MUTA_RT_N_THREADS_BATCH=
# Image input uses the selected model and its exact projector. `run.sh` and the local model
# catalog set this automatically; only externally managed one-model deployments should override
# it. Never pair a projector from a different model size/family.
# MUTA_RT_MMPROJ_PATH=models/core/mmproj-F16.gguf
# The lower/upper visual-token range is passed to llama-server. Chat admission reserves the
# upper bound, so do not raise MAX without also preserving prompt/reply room in N_CTX per lane.
# MUTA_RT_IMAGE_MIN_TOKENS=1024
# MUTA_RT_IMAGE_MAX_TOKENS=2048

# --- Muta Power (ON by default) -------------------------------------------------------
# Set the master switch to 0 only when a deployment must ignore host battery state.
# Thresholds are percentages and seconds; see docs/configuration.md for the full policy.
# MUTA_RT_POWER_OPTIMIZATION=1
# MUTA_RT_POWER_SENSOR_GRACE_S=120
# MUTA_RT_POWER_CRITICAL_PERCENTAGE=12
# MUTA_RT_POWER_CRITICAL_TIME_S=1800
